From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:09:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: Add MESA_KK_CACHE_BUILD_ID for development

The shader caches are named after the driver's build ID, so every build
starts with empty ones, and warming Rise of the Tomb Raider's take ten
minutes. Builds that leave the shader compiler alone can name them with
MESA_KK_CACHE_BUILD_ID instead and keep using an earlier build's.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_instance.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_instance.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_instance.c
index 90abd52..628c77c 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_instance.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_instance.c
@@ -135,6 +135,16 @@ kk_CreateInstance(const VkInstanceCreateInfo *pCreateInfo,
                  "UUID size mismatch");
    memcpy(instance->driver_build_sha, build_id_data(note), VK_UUID_SIZE);
 
+   /* For development: builds that leave the shader compiler alone can keep
+    * using the shader caches of an earlier one under the same name. Each
+    * build otherwise starts with empty caches. */
+   const char *cache_build_id = debug_get_option("MESA_KK_CACHE_BUILD_ID", NULL);
+   if (cache_build_id) {
+      blake3_hash hash;
+      _mesa_blake3_compute(cache_build_id, strlen(cache_build_id), hash);
+      memcpy(instance->driver_build_sha, hash, VK_UUID_SIZE);
+   }
+
    kk_process_debug_variable();
 
    *pInstance = kk_instance_to_handle(instance);
